GRN Variance Analysis - Technical Documentation
Use Case: Goods Receipt Note (GRN) Variance Analysis for Perishable Goods Payment Decisions

1. Executive Summary
1.1 Business Problem
In supply chain and procurement operations, organizations frequently encounter discrepancies between invoice quantities (what vendors claim to have delivered) and GRN quantities (what was actually received). This variance is particularly critical for perishable goods where:

Natural weight loss during transit is expected
Seasonal variations affect acceptable variance thresholds
Historical patterns determine what constitutes "normal" variance
Buyers need data-driven recommendations to approve or investigate payments
Manual variance analysis is time-consuming, inconsistent, and lacks the statistical rigor needed for informed payment decisions.

1.2 Solution Overview
The GRN Variance Analysis System is an AI-powered Azure Function that automatically analyzes invoice-to-GRN variances using historical data and LLM-based reasoning to provide actionable payment recommendations.

Technique	Purpose
Historical Data Analysis	Fetches past transaction records from SQL database
Statistical Metrics	Calculates percentiles, trends, and seasonal patterns
LLM Reasoning (Azure OpenAI)	Generates context-aware recommendations with justifications
Trend Visualization	Provides 12-month rolling variance trends
1.3 Key Capabilities
Historical Context: Analyzes up to 2 years (configurable) of transaction history
Statistical Analysis: Calculates mean, percentiles (5th, 25th, 50th, 75th, 95th), and seasonal patterns
AI-Powered Recommendations: Uses Azure OpenAI to classify products and recommend thresholds
Parallel Processing: Processes multiple line items concurrently using ThreadPoolExecutor
Monthly Trends: Provides 12-month rolling variance trend data
Dynamic Configuration: All field mappings and parameters are configurable via Azure Blob Storage
Comprehensive Validation: Pydantic-based input/output schema validation
